---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import operator from '../data/operator.json';
---
<Layout title="Privacy notice" description="How the CryptoOracle public website handles hosting data, cookies, external links and enquiries, and how to exercise your data protection rights.">
  <div class="wrap legal-wrap">
    <header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / LAST UPDATED 18 SEPTEMBER 2026</p><h1>Less data.<br /> <em>A clearer explanation.</em></h1><p>This notice covers the public CryptoOracle website. It explains the remaining processing even though this site has no visitor analytics, advertising, account registration or contact form.</p></header>
    <div class="privacy-summary"><span>No analytics</span><span>No advertising</span><span>No external fonts</span><span>No visitor-to-AI requests</span></div>
    <div class="reading-content legal-content">
      <section><h2>1. Who is responsible?</h2><address>{operator.name}<br /> {operator.street}<br /> {operator.postalCode} {operator.city}, {operator.country}</address><p>For privacy enquiries and rights requests: <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}>{operator.email || 'Contact address pending verification'}</a>. Further operator details are in the <a href="/legal/">legal notice</a>.</p></section>
      <section><h2>2. When you access this website</h2><p>Cloudflare delivers the pages and the public paper-portfolio API, and provides network protection. A request necessarily involves connection information such as your IP address, requested URL, time, browser information and technical routing data. Processing is required to deliver the page and protect the service against abuse.</p><p>The legal basis for necessary delivery and proportionate security processing is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR: our legitimate interest in providing a reliable, secure public research website. You are not required to register or submit information. Without the connection data, the site cannot be delivered.</p><p>The application does not maintain visitor profiles or a visitor database. Worker application logging and analytics are not enabled in this deployment. Cloudflare may nevertheless process infrastructure and security data when providing its service.</p></section>
      <section><h2>3. Hosting provider and international processing</h2><p>The hosting provider is Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. Cloudflare uses a global network, so processing is not represented as exclusively within the EU or EEA.</p><p>Cloudflare’s <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/" rel="external noreferrer">Data Processing Addendum</a> sets out processor obligations and safeguards for restricted transfers, including the EU Standard Contractual Clauses where applicable. Information on its infrastructure data processing and retention is available in the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="external noreferrer">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>. Details or copies of applicable safeguards may also be requested from the operator.</p><p>We do not export visitor-level request logs or keep a separate application copy. Provider-side processing and retention follow the service’s contractual obligations and documented purposes, including security and legal requirements. This notice does not promise zero provider retention.</p></section>
      <section><h2>4. Cookies and browser storage</h2><p>Our application does not set cookies, use local storage or session storage, or load advertising and analytics scripts. Display choices are kept in page memory, with shareable selections also represented in the page URL. The forecast journal sends the selected asset, horizon, model, status, page number or forecast ID to our same-origin public API to retrieve the matching records. The portfolio API receives the selected experiment ID; its account and decision filters run in the browser. These are ordinary delivery requests, not analytics events. The pages refresh when opened, when selections change, on manual refresh and about once a minute while visible. Requests omit credentials.</p><p>Cloudflare may use technically necessary security mechanisms, including storage associated with a security challenge. Those mechanisms are used to protect access rather than advertise or analyse behaviour. Necessary storage is assessed under Section 25(2) TDDDG. We do not add optional tracking or ask for consent to non-existent marketing features.</p></section>
      <section><h2>5. If you contact us</h2><p>Choosing an email link opens your own mail application. Sending a message is a separate, voluntary action. We use the address, message and any information you include to handle your enquiry. Please avoid unnecessary sensitive information.</p><p>General enquiries are handled under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, our legitimate interest in responding to correspondence; requests relating to a contract or steps before a contract fall under Article 6(1)(b). Correspondence is retained for as long as needed to resolve the matter and meet applicable legal retention or defence requirements. Continued need is reviewed when the matter is closed. This website itself does not store the correspondence.</p></section>
      <section><h2>6. Research models and external links</h2><p>The forecasts and model evaluations described here run in a separate research system. Browsing this site does not send your IP address, browsing choices or page content to TimesFM, JEV, Vercel AI Gateway or a cryptocurrency exchange. Published data is limited to selected research measurements, price forecasts and outcomes, numeric source checks, model and evidence hashes, and the project’s virtual portfolio balances, simulated trades and structured decision evidence. A Cloudflare D1 database holds the latest portfolio snapshots and learning summaries, and retains the public forecast claims, outcomes and numeric quality evidence; it does not contain visitor records, private manual holdings or raw headline text. Website requests are not forwarded to the private research server.</p><p>External services are linked, not embedded. Their sites receive a request only if you follow a link. Our pages use a no-referrer policy. The destination site then applies its own privacy practices.</p></section>
      <section><h2>7. Your rights</h2><p>Subject to the applicable conditions, you may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction and data portability. You may object to processing based on legitimate interests on grounds relating to your situation. If processing is ever based on consent, you may withdraw it for the future.</p><p>Contact the operator to exercise these rights. Requests are normally answered within one month; any lawful extension will be explained. We do not collect additional tracking data merely to identify past visitors.</p><p>You may complain to a supervisory authority, including the <a href="https://datenschutz-hamburg.de/" rel="external noreferrer">Hamburg Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information</a>, or the authority where you live, work or consider an infringement to have occurred.</p><p>This website does not profile visitors or make automated decisions about individuals that produce legal or similarly significant effects.</p></section>
      <section><h2>8. Changes</h2><p>This notice describes the current website and its public research APIs. Adding accounts, forms, analytics or other data processing requires an updated assessment and notice before those features are introduced. The date above identifies this version.</p></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
